h on for size!␀Enter Shop /^Challenge Opponent␀Your Xbox console cannot connect to Xbox Live.  Do you want to start the troubleshooter?␀Gamertag Banned␀The Xbox Live service is very busy.  Please try again later.␀This game session is no longer available.␀You were signed out of Xbox Live because another person signed in using your account.␀A required update is available for the Xbox Live service. You cannot connect to Xbox Live until the update is installed.␀This account is not current.  You need to update the account in Account Recovery.␀You have an important message from Xbox Live. You must read this message before you can sign in.␀Please change your Gamertag!␀You have a new Xbox Live message. Would you like to read it now?␀Network conditions may affect this game.␀Quit Demo␀Quit the demo?␀High Heat␀Powder Coat␀Powder Coat␀High Heat␀Mini Map Legend␀Sign in to Xbox Live␀Create New Account␀This demo is intended for promotional purposes only, and^may not be sold, rented or reproduced by any party.^^Any unauthorized use of this demo is prohibited^by applicable law.␀Mitsubishi, Eclipse, and Lancer Evolution names, emblems and body designs are trademarks and/or intellectual property rights of Mitsubishi Motors Corporation and used under license^to Electronic Arts Inc.^^"NISSAN" and the names, logos, marks and designs of the NISSAN products are trademarks and/or intellectual property rights^of NISSAN MOTOR CO., LTD. and used under license^to Electronic Arts Inc.^^SUBARU, IMPREZA, WRX and STi names, emblems and body designs are properties of Fuji Heavy Industries Ltd.^^The names and logos of all after market car part companies are^trademarks of their respective owners and are used^by permission.  All other trademarks are the property^of their respective owners.^^© 2004 Electronic Arts Inc. All rights reserved.␀"the Keys to Life vs. 15 Minutes of Fame"^Performed by Atmosphere^Recording courtesy of Rhymesayers Entertainment LLC, under^license to Epitaph Records^^"Switch/Twitch"^Performed by Fluke^Recording courtesy of One Little Indian Records^^"Notice of Eviction"^Performed by The Bronx^Recording courtesy of Ferret Music␀PUBLIC SERVICE ANNOUNCEMENT␀The cars shown in this game may be different in appearance^and performance than actual cars, and drivers shown in this^game may not be following automobile safety rules. When^driving a car in real life, please remember to be a safe^driver by wearing a seat belt, using your turn^signal and using good judgment.␀This shop is all about the looks.  You will find all new^categories with items like scissor doors, hydraulics,^audio components and spinners that really let you^showcase your ride.␀Your Car␀Opponent Car␀Showcase␀Circuit␀Street X␀Car Lot␀Graphics Shop␀Performance Shop␀Body Shop␀Car Specialties Shop␀Street X is tight racing on short tracks where quick reactions and nerves^of steel mean the difference between winning and losing. Accept^this challenge to experience a 3 lap race against 3 opponents where^you will have to fight an intense battle to gain the inside line.␀Change Parts␀Do you want to enter the Performance Tuning / Dyno track?␀Racing Category: %s␀Music Volume␀You Lost the Outrun!␀You Won the Outrun!␀Nissan␀Mitsubishi␀Chevrolet␀Generic␀240SX␀3000GT␀350Z␀A3␀Celica␀Civic␀Corolla␀Coupe␀Default␀Eclipse␀Escalade␀Firetruck␀Focus␀G35␀Golf␀Hummer H2␀Impreza␀WRX STi␀Integra␀IS 300␀Lancer␀Lancer␀MX-5␀Mustang GT␀Navigator␀Neon␀NSX␀Peugeot␀RSX␀RX-7␀RX-8␀S2000␀Skyline␀Supra␀Hyundai␀Outrun Challenge Accepted^Lose Them!␀Outrun Challenge Accepted^Catch Them!␀You have the Lead!␀You Lost the Lead!␀Please enter the pass code for %s␀Street X␀Explore Map Mode␀Race Map Mode␀Rotate␀Static␀Would you like to select this car?␀Tutorial Tip␀Steer With:␀directional button(s)␀$JOY_EVENT_FENG_PAD_LEFT_ALTERNATE$␀Preview␀Audio & Interiors is where you bring the "bling".  Select from a wide variety of "show" upgrades for your ride and enhance your^reputation on the streets.  You'll find all new categories with items^like scissor doors, hydraulics, audio components and spinners that^really let you showcase your ride.␀Get under the hood to individually tweak and tune over 20 different^performance settings for your cars.  Loosen up the suspension to^slide around the Drift tracks or shorten your gear ratios to get extra^acceleration off the line in a Drag.  Set up and save settings for each^car to get the maximum performance for each race type.␀Display SMS␀Network Troubleshooter␀Xbox Dashboard␀Account Recovery␀Update␀Read Now␀Read Later␀Play anyway␀Quit␀The car lot is the place to go when you need a new set of wheels␀Performance Shop Game Tip␀Choose from hundreds of custom paint colors, unique vinyls and decals in the Graphics Shop.␀Customize your car with hundreds of visual^upgrades to get the exact look you want.␀Audio Shop Game Tip␀Xbox Live Sign In Error␀Xbox Live Info␀%d unread messages␀Message %d of %d␀Rachel␀Rachel␀Rachel␀Rachel␀Rachel␀Rachel␀Rachel␀Rachel␀Rachel␀Rachel␀Messaging System␀Changing Controls␀Map Legend␀Outrun Mode␀Rules for Outrun Mode␀Hidden Shops␀The Race Breaker␀Magazine Photo Shoot␀Taking a Picture␀Magazine Cover Shot␀To enter shops or events, drive into the animated zone and press up on the SMS HUD, when prompted. To read incoming messages, press right on the SMS HUD when the mail icon appears.␀To change the steering controls, select Options and then select Player from the Pause Menu. Here you can cycle through the various steering preferences.␀Press down on the SMS HUD to access the Mini-map legend. This will show you what each icon on your map represents.␀Keep an eye out for other tuner cars on the road. They will be marked on your Mini-map as orange triangles. You can challenge these cars to an "Outrun" race by pressing up on the SMS HUD when prompted. When racing, the object is to gain the lead from your opponent and then lose them! You are free to take any route you want to try and beat them.␀The objective of an outrun race is to gain the lead and lose the opponent by creating a distance of over 300 meters.  You are free to^take any route you want when you are the leader.  If you are behind,^you need to catch the leader and pass them to take control of the race.␀Be sure to visit all the tuner shops in the world.  Most are marked on the mini map but "underground" race shop locations are tucked away "off the beaten path".  Keep a look out for side roads and alleys that can lead to special shops that carry the best parts and upgrades.␀The Race Breaker is a new addition to your nitrous system.  When you^fill your nitrous past 100%, you start collecting Race Breaker nitrous.^This adds even more boost and grip to your car and can make the^difference in a race.  Regular nitrous is identified by the blue color on^your nitrous HUD.  When it fills up, the green Race Breaker nitrous will^begin filling up on top of your regular nitrous.␀That was some nice driving!  There's a photographer who wants to get a shot of the winning car for Underground magazine.  You've got 45^seconds to reach his location before he takes off to find another driver.^The location is marked by a flashing yellow star on your mini map, now hurry!␀Congratulations!^Your car will be featured on the cover of the Need for Speed‚^Underground 2 magazine!␀That's a sweet ride you just picked up!  There's a photographer who^wants to snap a picture of your car for a tuner magazine cover.  His^location is marked with a yellow star on your mini map.␀From: %s␀Subject: %s␀Welcome to Need for Speed Underground 2.^This demo lets you experience a small part of the high speed,^fast paced world of tuner culture available in the full version.^^^^^Coming November 2004␀Do you want to select this body kit?␀AUDIO␀PLAYER␀GAMEPLAY␀DEBUG␀DEBUG Rendering␀DEBUG Physics␀Discover the living, breathing^world of tuner culture in Need for Speed‚ Underground 2.^Taking place in a massive,^free-roaming city featuring^five distinct interconnected^neighborhoods, Need for Speed^Underground 2 delivers an immersive game world^where the streets are your menus.␀Disqualified␀waiting␀received␀Resolution␀Level Of Detail␀Customize Display Settings␀Default Settings␀Low␀Medium␀High␀Display␀Are you sure you want to exit to the Xbox Dashboard and create a new Xbox Live‚  Account?␀February␀March␀April␀May␀June␀July␀August␀September␀October␀November␀December␀Friends List␀All␀Players List␀Friend Requests␀Blocked␀Car Specialties Shop␀Game Type␀Ranked␀Unranked␀Start Race␀Primary␀Secondary␀© 2004 Electronic Arts Inc. All rights reserved.␀Select␀Using online persona '%s'...␀Select Car␀Race Countdown:  %d␀Laps␀Incoming Mobile Message␀Free-Roaming City␀Performance Tuning␀New Gameplay Modes␀Visual Customization␀Compete Online␀Races can happen anytime, anywhere␀Fine-tune every aspect of your car␀Hone your skills in a number of driving disciplines␀New personalization options and tons of new parts␀Challenging the world␀Each car lot will have a different inventory, so you might have to do some exploring to find the model you want. There are over 30 models from some of the best known manufacturers on the tuning scene, including Nissan, Mazda, Toyota, Subaru, Mitsubishi, Ford, and more.␀Here are 2 examples of some tricked out rides that you can build^in the full version of Underground 2.␀Each car lot will have a different inventory, so you might have to do^some exploring to find the model you want. There are over 30^models from some of the best known manufacturers on the^tuning scene, including Nissan, Mazda, Toyota,^Subaru, Mitsubishi, Ford, and more.^^Here are 2 examples of some tricked out rides^that you can build in the full version of Underground 2.␀In the full version of Underground 2, the paint shop is the place^to go to add that personal touch to your ride. Make your car^stand out from the crowd with a special paint or cool custom^vinyl. You can also come here to apply your favorite^manufacturer decal to your car.^^Here is a small sample of colors and paint styles that you^can apply to your car.␀The Body Shop carries a wide range of parts to customize the^look of your car; including wheels, spoilers, hoods, wide body kits^and more. You will find hundreds of brand new designs in^Underground 2 which range from mild to wild!^^Here are 2 examples of some tricked out rides that you can^build in the full version of Underground 2.␀Current Car␀Tuner Car 1␀Tuner Car 2␀Reset to default settings?␀Car Reflection Update Rate␀Car Reflection Detail␀Car Shadow␀Car Headlight␀Car Lighting␀Crowds␀World Detail␀Road Reflection Detail␀Meters␀Time:␀Rookie␀Novice␀Intermediate␀Skilled␀Advanced␀Veteran␀Expert␀Professional␀Legendary␀Elite␀Retrieving rankings board data from the server.␀Incoming Mobile Message␀$JOY_EVENT_FENG_CANCEL$ Back   $JOY_EVENT_FENG_SELECT$ Select Car␀Next␀Mini Map Legend␀Graphics Shop␀Help␀Back␀Select␀On␀Off␀From: %s␀Simon␀Simon␀Simon␀EA GAMES‚ TRAX␀Resume Test Run␀Tune Settings␀Test Run␀Store Settings␀Restore Settings␀Quit Tuning␀Dyno Run␀Suspension␀Drivetrain␀Aerodynamics␀Tires & Brakes␀ECU␀Turbo␀Nitrous␀Configure your settings␀Press enter to assign a new key or button␀Press a button to use for this function␀Steering (Left)␀Steering (Right)␀Back / Reverse␀Shift Up␀Shift Down␀Handbrake␀Nitrous Boost␀Camera␀Look back␀Pause␀Engage Mechanism␀World Map␀Hydraulic Bounce␀Hydraulic Pressurize␀Throttle␀Light Trails␀Light Glow␀Animated Texture␀Particle System␀Motion Blur␀Race Type:␀Distance:␀Best Lap:␀Comments:␀There was a problem retrieving rank data from the server.^Please try again later.␀URL Race␀Comment: %s␀For this you need N2O. No... make that 2 cans, 2 of the big ones!␀View DVD Covers␀View Magazines␀View Signed Sponsors␀Reward Options␀Front Springs␀Rear Springs␀Front Shocks␀Rear Shocks␀Front Sway Bar␀Rear Sway Bar␀Steering Ratio␀Final Drive Ratio␀1st Gear␀2nd Gear␀3rd Gear␀4th Gear␀5th Gear␀6th Gear␀Rate of Depletion␀Nitrous Torque␀Brake Bias␀Front Tire Grip␀Rear Tire Grip␀Front Downforce␀Rear Downforce␀ECU Torque Curve␀Turbo Torque